## Substantive Content

### Framing
Explicitly positioned as a "pre-read" — an input to a broader, evolving National AI Strategy process, not a finalised policy. Recommendations are described as preliminary.

### "#AIforAll" framing
The strategy frames India's AI approach around inclusive growth — AI as a tool for development across sectors (health, agriculture, education, smart mobility/transport, smart cities) rather than primarily as an industrial-competitiveness play (contrast with how some other jurisdictions framed early AI strategy around economic competition).

### Structural themes (as discernible from extraction)
- Sector-wise application areas for AI (the "five focus sectors" approach commonly associated with #AIforAll: healthcare, agriculture, education, smart cities/mobility, smart infrastructure).
- Barriers to AI adoption identified, including data access/quality, skilling, and research ecosystem gaps.
- Recommendations framed as inputs for further deliberation, not binding commitments.

