## Analytical Significance for PRIS Research

### For P1 (AI Governance SLR) and P2 (DPI Governance, JSIS)
NITI_7 (2018) represents **India's "year zero" for AI policy** — analogous to RBI_4 (2017) as the BFSI sector's "year zero." Both show technology framed initially around opportunity/inclusion rather than risk/governance, with risk-based framing emerging only in 2024-2025 instruments (RBI_3, RBI_FREE_AI_2025, MeitY_1, MeitY_2). This 2018→2025 arc (opportunity framing → risk/governance framing) is a useful narrative spine for P1's historical contextualisation of India's AI governance evolution.

### Coordination / Parallelism Pattern
Existing nodes: [[07_Institutions/Corpus/NITI_Aayog/NITI_3]], [[07_Institutions/Corpus/NITI_Aayog/NITI_6]]. Pattern: **Sequential evolution (intra-institution)** — NITI_7 (2018, strategy/discussion paper) likely precedes and informs NITI_3/NITI_6 (later, more developed outputs); exact relationship to be confirmed in a future session by reading NITI_3/NITI_6 content against NITI_7.

